# Veripsa release gate (auto-discovered). One gate per file -> two PRs adding gates add two FILES, never a
# shared line -> no false merge conflict on registration. register_gate is defined in run_gates.sh.
# Format: register_gate <test> <marker> <name> <ok_blurb> <desc> [tail]
register_gate "tests/test_install_cap_knob.py" "INSTALL-CAP KNOB GATE: PASS" "install-cap knob (VERIPSA_APP_INSTALLATIONS_CAP replaces the hardcoded 500 ceiling in list_app_installations; truncation alert fires content-free when the cap is hit)" "install-cap knob: VERIPSA_APP_INSTALLATIONS_CAP (default 500, min 1) replaces the hardcoded 500 in list_app_installations; a bad knob fails LOUD at startup (env_int); when the returned installation count reaches the cap a content-free WARNING fires with count + knob name only (no tenant ids, no org names) so the operator knows to raise the cap; when below the cap the key is resolved (re-armed)" "install-cap knob (P2-3): a public Marketplace App with more than 500 tenants would silently ceiling at 500 -- boot_reconcile and for_account would never see tenants beyond the cap. VERIPSA_APP_INSTALLATIONS_CAP makes the ceiling operator-controlled and fail-LOUD on misconfiguration; the truncation alert tells the operator when to raise it, content-free (count + knob name only -- no tenant ids, no org names, no installation details)" 18
